{"schema":"cr/v1","tip":"b006031931bd6fb59cee60ac91801b7e78fd6d2b","base":"cd90c16bfa27467a4189a1335ab2046b5775bfc1","branch":"wu/E-RGUARD/w3-inbox-channel","committer":"vuluu <quangvu.luu92@gmail.com>","timestamp":1794665218,"verdict":"FAIL","blockers":0,"importants":2,"code_diff_hash":"5565119e7a67a8a14fffac0be6fc6056cfb2ad66","round":1,"scope":"full","findings":[{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:107-121","claim":"A file whose name equals a well-formed header id and a valid kind but whose id carries a character consume's regex refuses (a space, a tab, a control character) is printed by watch on every arm, consume rejects it as 'bad id', and because watch always takes the first valid file in glob order every later message is starved until the owner moves the file by hand.","severity":"important","evidence":"Reproduced in /tmp: files named '0000000001-e\\u001b[31mvil.msg' and '1700000006-a b.msg' (headers matching, kind NOTE) were printed as MSG by watch; 'consume 1700000006-a b' exits 2 'bad id'; three arms printed the junk file while a real posted message behind it was never shown; the router cannot ack it (scripts/router-guard.jq:33 consume shape and scripts/router-inbox.sh:134 refuse the same characters) nor delete it (no verb; the guard denies rm), so a hostile name jams the channel."},{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:58-59","claim":"show bounds the body to 80 lines but never to bytes, so one body line of any length is printed whole: a 5 MiB single-line body written straight into the inbox produced 5,242,955 bytes of watch output (bytes=65536 in the header), bypassing the 4,000-byte cap that post enforces at line 85.","severity":"important","evidence":"Reproduced in /tmp: a 5,242,941-byte file with 5 header lines and one unbroken body line gave `sh scripts/router-inbox.sh watch 1 | wc -c` = 5,242,955; the same size in short lines prints 80 lines (1,026 bytes), so only the line bound holds. The script's own comment at lines 11-16 and DEC-57 promise the inbox is writable by any local process, and the post cap is the only bound on the body."}],"refuted":[{"location":".claude/settings.json:22","claim":"The new Bash(scripts/router-inbox.sh *) allow rule lets the router post to its own channel.","why":"The PreToolUse guard wired with no matcher at .claude/settings.json:33-43 runs on every Bash call and scripts/router-guard.jq:33 has no 'post' alternative, so a probe of 'scripts/router-inbox.sh post e REPORT hi' is denied; the allow rule only skips a permission prompt, it does not bypass the hook. Kept as a nit against the wildcard, not a bypass."},{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:106","claim":"watch follows a symlink out of the inbox in the window between the -L/-f checks and the sed that reads it.","why":"A swapped link must still carry a line 1 exactly 'id: <file stem>' and a closed kind to be printed (scripts/router-inbox.sh:109-115), and a process able to write the inbox already holds the router's uid and can read the same file directly; reproduced links and forged files are skipped. The residual TOCTOU is inside DEC-57's accepted trust model (docs/decisions/router.html:184)."},{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:87-94","claim":"Two concurrent posters can clobber each other or leave a partial message the watcher sees.","why":"mktemp gives each writer its own dotfile and mv renames it into place atomically; a 50-poster probe in /tmp produced 50 distinct ids, 50 whole bodies and no orphan, and the .new.* dotfile is outside the *.msg glob (scripts/router-inbox.sh:105)."},{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:103-129","claim":"A killed watcher loses the message it was about to print.","why":"watch never writes or consumes; it prints and exits, so a killed watcher leaves the file for the next arm (test a_killed_watcher_loses_nothing and the /tmp probe agree)."},{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:119-128","claim":"An unconsumed message is delivered more than once per arm.","why":"The watcher exits after the first valid file (line 121), so each arm prints at most once; three /tmp arms printed the same id once each and the fourth arm timed out only after consume."},{"location":"scripts/router-guard.jq:30-34","claim":"post or another verb can be smuggled through the plain-word guard with quotes, metacharacters, a newline, '..' or a second command.","why":"Probed every shape: quotes, ;, &&, |, >, $(), backticks, embedded newline, ../, x/y, a double space, an env assignment, a leading sh, 8-digit watch and trailing words are all denied; the four documented shapes are allowed and the new tests/router.rs cases pass (59 passed)."},{"location":"scripts/router-guard.jq:33","claim":"Admitting 'watch 0' leaves the router a poll it can loop.","why":"watch 0 is one immediate scan then TIMEOUT exit 1 (scripts/router-inbox.sh:99-128), i.e. one bounded tool call, not a loop; no shipped text tells the router to arm it, and the owner's no-heartbeat rule is about the router scheduling itself."},{"location":"skills/keel-router/SKILL.md:1","claim":"The two skill trees drifted or the decision index was not renumbered.","why":"diff -r skills/keel-router .claude/skills/keel-router is empty; docs/decisions/decisions-index.html:13 says next free DEC-58 and its router row now ends DEC-55 - DEC-57, matching docs/decisions/router.html:13 and the new #dec-57 row."},{"location":"docs/decisions/router.html:181","claim":"DEC-57 does not really amend DEC-55, so both the old and new report rules stand.","why":"DEC-57's Lineage at docs/decisions/router.html:185 records the amendment of DEC-55's report sentence, in the file's append-only convention (meta at line 10); the missing inline marker is recorded as a nit, not a second rule."},{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:21-22","claim":"A body with invalid UTF-8 breaks post or the wake.","why":"Post with stdin 'caf\\377\\376 bad' stored the bytes and watch printed them unchanged (od: 63 61 66 ff fe); the script exports LC_ALL=C and says at lines 21-22 that a body may carry bytes that are not UTF-8, so no crash, no loss, and the raw bytes are intended."},{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:31-33","claim":"A worker's worktree copy posts to its own worktree instead of the main checkout's inbox.","why":"git rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir from the script's own directory resolves the main git dir and dirname gives the main checkout; test a_worktree_copy_resolves_the_main_checkouts_inbox passes in the 21-case run."},{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:85","claim":"A refused oversized post leaves a message file or a dotfile behind.","why":"The size check at line 85 runs before mktemp at line 87; the test post_refuses_an_oversized_body_before_any_file_exists passes and the /tmp probe left no .msg and no .new.*."},{"location":"docs/decisions/router.html:184","claim":"The skill promises a worker report where a DSH worker cannot post (a plain-directory workspace).","why":"DEC-57:184 states a plain-directory workspace (workspace-write) cannot post, and SKILL.md:254 states a linked-worktree worker runs danger-full-access while a plain-directory one runs workspace-write; both skill bullets also say a worker that posts nothing is invisible, so no liveness is promised."}],"nits":[{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:57-59","finding":"The MSG header prints from, kind and the id raw; only the body passes through clean(), so a forged 'from: \\u001b[2Jevil' or an id holding ESC reaches the router's terminal as an escape sequence (reproduced with od: MSG ... from=033 [ 2 J evil)."},{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:155-159","finding":"status counts a zero-byte or header-less regular *.msg as pending and names it oldest, although watch will never deliver it; the probe showed pending=1 oldest=3333333333-empty.msg while watch timed out, so status can report a message that cannot arrive."},{"location":"tests/router_inbox.rs:307-320","finding":"The symlink test cannot prove what its name claims: the symlink target's first line is 'SECRET-NOT-A-MESSAGE', not 'id: 0000000001-evil', so the header check at scripts/router-inbox.sh:110 skips it even with the -L check removed; a target holding a matching header would be the failing case."},{"location":"tests/router_inbox.rs:203-218","finding":"two_concurrent_posts_both_land_whole_with_distinct_ids asserts only distinct ids and pending=2, never a body, so a torn or swapped body would pass the test named for that contract."},{"location":"tests/router.rs:150","finding":"The settings-driven allowed-shapes loop maps '.claude/settings.json:22' Bash(scripts/router-inbox.sh *) to 'watch 6600' only, so it cannot see that the same allow pattern also matches 'post'; the hook still denies post (scripts/router-guard.jq:30-34), but settings and guard are no longer one shape list and the test note's 'settings allow exactly the shapes the guard admits' is false."},{"location":"skills/keel-router/SKILL.md:326-331","finding":"The no-heartbeat bullet says the router 'runs no loop, timer or reminder' while requiring it to re-arm watch 6600 on every wake; the watcher's own 6,600 s bounded exit renews that wake (about 13 a day), which worker-ops.md:230 and DEC-57:184 state and SKILL.md does not, so the file a router reads states the cost as zero."},{"location":"skills/keel-router/references/worker-ops.md:199-237","finding":"The channel section never says read/ is never pruned or that .router/ is unbacked; only DEC-57:184 (and the T3 result) states the growth and that deleting .router/ drops pending messages, where a router operating the channel may not read it."},{"location":"docs/decisions/router.html:181","finding":"DEC-57's Context says 'The 27-check hermetic test' while its Lineage at line 185 says 'the 28-check test'; plan, tests/router_inbox.rs:3 and the plan's acceptance say 27 and the result says 28, so the count a later reader cites is inconsistent."},{"location":"docs/decisions/router.html:181-185","finding":"DEC-57 says it 'Amends DEC-55's report sentence', but DEC-55's row and decisions-index.html:22 still state the old rule (a DSH worker's report is its transcript) with no amendment marker, so a reader who follows the index to DEC-55 meets the superseded rule first."},{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:142-148","finding":"With two consume calls racing on one id, the loser's mv writes 'mv: .../x.msg: No such file or directory' to stderr before the CONSUMED-ALREADY line (reproduced); the fallback should silence mv or test the source again."},{"location":"tests/router_inbox.rs:286","finding":"The armed-watcher and killed-watcher cases use a fixed 200 ms sleep as synchronization (also line 370) against the testing charter's no-sleep rule; neither result would change without it because watch checks at once and a watcher killed before it starts still loses nothing."}],"fleet":{"dimensions":["correctness","efficiency"],"finders":1,"verifiers":1,"verifier_model":"deepseek-flash","candidates":{"blocker":0,"important":2,"nit":11},"by_finder":{"correctness":{"found":13,"verified":13},"efficiency":{"found":0,"verified":0}},"waivers":[],"mode":"single independent reviewer; subagent delegation is disabled in this session, so finder and verifier are the same fresh session; altitude not spawned because the diff's code paths (tests/router.rs, tests/router_inbox.rs) resolve to one module (tests/), and the script, guard, settings and skill text are outside code_paths and judged by hand as the brief asks","note":"cr code_diff_hash binds tests/router.rs and tests/router_inbox.rs only; scripts/router-inbox.sh, scripts/router-guard.jq, .claude/settings.json, .keel/config.toml and the skill/decision text were reviewed by hand and by execution in /tmp and are NOT covered by the hash"}}
